2026-09-17 08:49:37,146 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "v", "argument_id": "3baaae4c-a5f5-4be6-9da3-78ca297c7252", "id": "619c2fcc-7e4f-46e4-9a77-81ee9f126c2c", "reason": "V will not formally confirm tolerance until the package is genuinely concrete and verifiable, not merely agreed in framework. If the concretized numbers/timelines/mechanisms remain symbolic, or if C's enterprise/decentralization demands dilute V's welfare, housing, equality and reduced-profit-seeking commitments, or if V's institutionalized budget/reform role is not truly non-bypassable, V will withhold its formal abstention in the PM vote \u2014 so S's desired effect of securing V's formal tolerance may fail or be limited."}
2026-09-17 08:49:37,147 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "kd", "argument_id": "3baaae4c-a5f5-4be6-9da3-78ca297c7252", "id": "75226c81-2940-4176-8e17-041f2cb0d2db", "reason": "The S+C+MP package (147 seats) is fragile and V-dependent: it needs 28 non-NO in the PM vote, which essentially requires V's formal abstention. But V has made strong visible binding influence (and even participation) a hard condition, while C only offers tolerance - if V's demands are not met, V will not abstain and the package fails the 175-test. Excluding KD's 22 seats makes this package far less robust than the mitten S+C+MP+KD (169), which needs only 6 non-NO and keeps V out of government entirely, better serving S's own stated goal of keeping V out of government."}
2026-09-17 08:49:37,147 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "m", "argument_id": "3baaae4c-a5f5-4be6-9da3-78ca297c7252", "id": "833a1728-12ca-4a35-9571-4908df5aeb97", "reason": "The S-led package hinges entirely on V's formal abstention in the PM vote, which V has made conditional on binding welfare/housing/equality/profit commitments that directly conflict with C's enterprise/decentralization commitments and MP's binding climate demands; reconciling these into a single verifiable package is fragile, and if V's base forces a NO vote or V withholds abstention the PM vote fails (NO=202>175) and the whole construction collapses."}
2026-09-17 08:49:37,148 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "l", "argument_id": "3baaae4c-a5f5-4be6-9da3-78ca297c7252", "id": "b455dbf4-5382-44bd-bfe0-5c3f792424f6", "reason": "The S+C+MP+V package rests on a fundamental internal contradiction that the round cannot resolve: V has made formal participation in the government a hard condition for its support, while C has committed to V only as a tolerating support party outside the government. Because V's formal abstention in the PM vote and its tolerance for the budget path are therefore not secured, the claimed 'binding, verifiable' package and the credible 176 budget majority are not credible \u2014 the round cannot lock a package that its own key partner (V) refuses to accept in the form C offers, so the desired effect of a stable, verifiable S-led government is not achieved."}
2026-09-17 08:49:37,148 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "sd", "argument_id": "3baaae4c-a5f5-4be6-9da3-78ca297c7252", "id": "f42b063f-16a6-41b7-964d-0d7eb56e4f7b", "reason": "The claimed 'binding and verifiable' package is not secured because it rests on V's formal abstention/tolerance, yet V has made government participation a hard condition for letting through an S-led government (V: 'kr\u00e4vt regeringsdeltagande om partiets mandat beh\u00f6vs') while C categorically refuses V in government. S's proposal gives V only a tolerance role outside government, leaving this V\u2013C contradiction unresolved, so V's formal abstention and the claimed 176 budget path are not verifiable and the package can collapse at the PM vote or the first budget."}
