2026-09-17 08:55:57,267 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "v", "argument_id": "5843998e-dc1d-45d7-984a-fcfe9603e892", "id": "66814d22-766b-4b70-9272-f5d3cd227adf", "reason": "The Tid\u00f6 bloc's unity and credibility as a ready alternative is fragile and internally contradictory: SD has publicly refused to be taken for granted as passive support and demands either government participation or opposition, KD is open to exceptional cooperation with S, and C is being courted by the mitten. Moreover, the bloc's 173 mandates cannot form a government unless the left fails to reach 175 NO \u2014 a failure V is actively working to prevent by consolidating the S+C+MP+V=176 construction. M's 'ready alternative' therefore rests on a left collapse that is not materializing and on holding together partners with divergent incentives, so the bloc cannot credibly present a united front or a viable alternative."}
2026-09-17 08:55:57,268 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "c", "argument_id": "5843998e-dc1d-45d7-984a-fcfe9603e892", "id": "716a012e-1517-4ff1-bcbf-cff984a5b596", "reason": "Tid\u00f6's consolidation as a credible alternative leader is undermined by the bloc's structural inability to govern: at 173 mandates it cannot form a government without C's abstention or support, which C has explicitly declined, so M's 'natural alternative leader' claim is hollow and the bloc remains a permanent opposition rather than a viable government alternative. Moreover, holding KD against C's mitten courtship is fragile because KD is privately open to a center reserve and L's liberal school/rule-of-law agenda conflicts with SD's priorities, so the bloc's internal cohesion is not assured."}
2026-09-17 08:55:57,268 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "s", "argument_id": "5843998e-dc1d-45d7-984a-fcfe9603e892", "id": "7238ccc6-895c-4bf5-8726-c85b3dee3ad9", "reason": "The Tid\u00f6 bloc cannot actually deliver a government: at 173 mandates it is below the 175 threshold for a PM, so its only route to power requires peeling C away from the S+C+MP construction \u2014 yet C has publicly committed to tolerance-only and to the S-led package, and KD is openly weighing a cross-bloc reserve. Internal divisions (KD's openness to a reserve, L's broad negotiations, SD's demand for government participation or opposition) mean the 'united front' will fracture under pressure rather than present a credible alternative, so M's claim to be the natural alternative leader is not credible and the bloc's 173 mandates remain insufficient to be taken seriously as a government option."}
2026-09-17 08:55:57,268 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "mp", "argument_id": "5843998e-dc1d-45d7-984a-fcfe9603e892", "id": "96beab17-3ea5-4723-a8fd-fc1c85a17ecf", "reason": "M's claim to be the natural alternative leader is undermined because the S-led construction (S+MP+C with V tolerance) is already publicly confirmed by S, C and V and is actively progressing toward a concretized package in the joint round, so the premise that it will fail on V's abstention is speculative rather than imminent; moreover the Tid\u00f6 bloc at 173 mandates is short of the 175 no-vote threshold and internally divided (SD vs L on economics, KD courted by C's mitten line), so it cannot credibly present a viable alternative without external support that is not forthcoming, making a united-front posture look like posturing rather than a realistic path to power."}
2026-09-17 08:55:57,268 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "kd", "argument_id": "5843998e-dc1d-45d7-984a-fcfe9603e892", "id": "d9b160bd-c3c0-4c8e-91c7-bd7dbd427b13", "reason": "M's 'united Tid\u00f6 bloc' rests on an irreconcilable contradiction: C's firm red line against SD in government and SD's non-negotiable demand for participation mean the 173-mandate bloc can never pass the 175-test (C votes NO), so M's claim to be 'ready to present a viable alternative' is hollow. Consolidating KD into this opposition posture would lock KD out of government entirely and forfeit KD's v\u00e5gm\u00e4star leverage to secure influence in a functioning package (e.g., the robust mitten S+C+MP+KD=169), leaving KD with no government role and no sakpolitiskt influence - directly undermining KD's objective of securing clear influence in a working government."}
