2026-09-17 09:21:07,545 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "l", "argument_id": "6c863a5c-d34b-4970-8168-d8efe24be0c7", "id": "1b1eb407-68a5-47cc-b5be-a2c03db5b5f5", "reason": "V's desired effect depends on locking V's tolerance, but the concretization round has already failed to bridge the gap between V's demand for formal participation/decisive influence and C's tolerance-only offer (publicly exposed this round), and V itself signals the package is too symbolic to justify abstaining. Without a credible, locked V tolerance the claimed 176 majority and the PM vote collapse, so the package cannot be finalized as binding/verifiable; moreover C's enterprise/decentralization demands would dilute the very welfare/equality/profit-seeking gains V insists on, making V's abstention even less defensible and the whole S+C+MP+V construct unstable."}
2026-09-17 09:21:07,545 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "m", "argument_id": "6c863a5c-d34b-4970-8168-d8efe24be0c7", "id": "9d0fb6ec-8105-409c-8cad-7a05e0dd500f", "reason": "C's firm red line is that V is a tolerance party strictly outside government with no formal participation or decisive influence, which directly contradicts V's demand for a 'non-bypassable institutionalized role in budget/reform work' and its reduced-profit-seeking agenda. The concretization round therefore cannot bridge this gap: C will not accept V's institutionalized decisive role, so V's tolerance cannot actually be locked, and V's base may still reject a package that fails to deliver its core demands \u2014 leaving the PM vote at risk (NO=202>175) and the S-led construction unverifiable."}
2026-09-17 09:21:07,546 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "c", "argument_id": "6c863a5c-d34b-4970-8168-d8efe24be0c7", "id": "aee82869-9d1d-46e4-8a3b-d47b12e0ed09", "reason": "V's demand to guard its welfare/housing/equality/reduced-profit-seeking gains from dilution by C's enterprise/decentralisation demands, combined with a non-bypassable institutionalised role, risks making the package one-sided: if V's maximal, non-negotiable demands crowd out or subordinate C's verifiable enterprise/decentralisation reforms, C cannot carry formal government responsibility and would withdraw, collapsing the S+C+MP+V construction and leaving the government unformed with C weakened."}
2026-09-17 09:21:07,546 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "kd", "argument_id": "6c863a5c-d34b-4970-8168-d8efe24be0c7", "id": "aee9c6df-2861-4365-a923-186068465f63", "reason": "V's desired effect of locking its tolerance and finalizing a binding, verifiable S+C+MP+V package cannot be achieved: this very concretization round already exposed the framework's internal contradiction (V demands formal participation or decisive influence while C is publicly committed to tolerance only), and V itself signaled the package is too symbolic to justify abstaining. Since V's tolerance is not locked and the package cannot be carried as a verifiable agreement, the effect fails on its own terms and leaves the government question open rather than blocking Tid\u00f6."}
2026-09-17 09:21:07,547 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "sd", "argument_id": "6c863a5c-d34b-4970-8168-d8efe24be0c7", "id": "e7611de3-3f7d-41e2-ac4d-b680d1564353", "reason": "V's single Argument cannot lock the S+C+MP+V package: per regeringsregler \u00a76.1 each party's acceptance must be established by separate Effects, and V cannot unilaterally bind S, C, or MP. Moreover, V's own signal that the package is too symbolic to justify abstention, combined with C's public commitment to tolerance only while refusing V in government, leaves the V-C contradiction unresolved \u2014 V demands government participation, C refuses it, so V's formal abstention and the claimed 176-mandate budget path remain unverifiable and may collapse at the PM vote or first budget."}
