2026-09-17 09:35:54,769 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "sd", "argument_id": "3d69e7c6-c9c8-43fd-bb0e-459127498b75", "id": "6da6ec97-94e0-4315-b37a-2a70a8b5f37e", "reason": "MP cannot unilaterally bind S, C, or V per regeringsregler \u00a76.1/\u00a79, and MP's championing of V's substantive demands does not resolve the core V-C contradiction: V demands a non-bypassable institutionalized role (stated but not accepted by C), while C refuses V in government and commits only to tolerance. V has already signalled the package is 'too symbolic' to justify abstaining, and MP's own green package adds policy concessions without giving V the formal role it demands, so V's abstention is not locked and the 175-test path remains unverifiable."}
2026-09-17 09:35:54,770 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "v", "argument_id": "3d69e7c6-c9c8-43fd-bb0e-459127498b75", "id": "7603f5f9-7214-424e-a2cb-43f3eee1831f", "reason": "MP's package locks climate commitments with concrete figures, tidplan and independent follow-up, but V's own substantive demands (welfare, housing, equality, reduced profit-seeking) are only 'championed' without the same binding, verifiable mechanisms and without V's institutionalized, non-bypassable role in budget/reform work. Since V's red line is that tolerance is conditional on a concrete, verifiable, enforceable package that includes that institutionalized role and binding mechanisms for V's own demands \u2014 not only climate \u2014 MP's desired effect of securing V's abstention may fail: V cannot justify abstaining on a package where its own demands remain symbolic while only climate is concretized, so the S-led government may still not pass the 175-test."}
2026-09-17 09:35:54,771 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "l", "argument_id": "3d69e7c6-c9c8-43fd-bb0e-459127498b75", "id": "d08a4721-ae68-4de7-bd73-f0b5dbb135a5", "reason": "MP's championing of V's substantive demands does not resolve the V-C contradiction: V has explicitly demanded a non-bypassable institutionalized role or formal participation (effect c7e19c05), not merely policy wins, while C has publicly committed to tolerance-only (c15fe751). V has already signaled the package is 'too symbolic' to justify abstaining (d1701488, 5f9f0deb), so MP's substantive additions do not lock V's abstention. Moreover, the draft package is not binding on S, C, or MP (179d5e1a), and MP's championing of V's welfare/equality/reduced-profit elements directly conflicts with C's enterprise and decentralization elements, risking C's withdrawal and collapsing the package rather than securing the 175-test."}
2026-09-17 09:35:54,771 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "m", "argument_id": "3d69e7c6-c9c8-43fd-bb0e-459127498b75", "id": "d2950bbd-5431-4b86-a400-0cfb876e313e", "reason": "MP's package does not resolve the V-C contradiction that is the actual blocker: V has publicly demanded a non-bypassable institutionalized role (formal participation or decisive influence in budget/reform work), while C's red line is V outside government with no formal participation. MP's concrete climate figures and championing of V's substantive policy demands give V policy wins but NOT the institutionalized role V insists on - and V has already signalled that a package without such a role is 'too symbolic' to justify abstaining. Since C will not concede the institutionalized role and V will not abstain without it, V's tolerance is not locked, so the S+MP+C (147) government still fails the 175-test (NO=Tid\u00f6 bloc=173 only if V abstains; if V votes NO, NO=202>175)."}
2026-09-17 09:35:54,771 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "kd", "argument_id": "3d69e7c6-c9c8-43fd-bb0e-459127498b75", "id": "f8612c23-7074-4b4b-861f-842d8794a0d9", "reason": "MP's package cannot lock V's abstention because it does not resolve the core V-C contradiction: V's stated demand is a non-bypassable institutionalized role or formal participation, not merely substantive policy wins. By championing V's welfare, housing, equality and reduced-profit-taking demands, MP makes the package unpalatable to C, whose tolerance-only commitment and center-right base cannot accept reduced profit-taking - so C may withdraw and V still lacks the institutionalized role it demands, leaving V's abstention unlocked and the S-led government unable to pass the 175-test."}
